// same-type retag: no reflect frames, no boxing, no type dispatch.
//
// Dispatch shape mirrors the reflective decoder exactly: the scalar families
// resolve by underlying kind (so a named type over int64 decodes through the
// same conversion the reflective kind switch performs — nativeSlot carries
// ~int members and the shared bind overloads require the same latitude),
// while the array-kind builtin members resolve on exact type like the
// reflective decoder's inner switch. Value parity is pinned to
// convertVariantToGoTypeReflectValue and the reflective Variant return
// matrix (GDExtensionVariantPtrFromReflectValue): every closure body performs
// the same conversion expression as its reflective twin, making parity a
// code-equality invariant. Engine dependency is likewise unchanged: the
// To*/Encoder calls require a live engine, exactly like the reflective path.

